---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy of Avorix GmbH — information on the processing of your personal data in accordance with GDPR.">
 <section class="pt-32 pb-24 px-6">
    <div style="max-width:var(--spalte-text)">
      <h1 class="mb-8" style="color:var(--druck)">Privacy Policy</h1>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">1. Privacy at a Glance</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">General Information</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        The following information provides a simple overview of what happens to your personal data
        when you visit this website. Personal data is any data that can be used to personally identify you.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">Data Collection on This Website</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Who is responsible for data collection on this website?</strong><br />
        Data processing on this website is carried out by the website operator:<br /><br />
        AVORIX GmbH<br />
        Fallenbrunnen 14<br />
        88045 Friedrichshafen, Germany<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@avorix.de" class="typo-link">info@avorix.de</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">2. Hosting</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        This website is hosted by an external service provider. Personal data collected on this website
        is stored on the host's servers. This may include IP addresses, contact requests, meta and
        communication data, contract data, contact details, names, website access, and other data
        generated through a website.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        Our host is:<br />
        Hostinger International Ltd.<br />
        61 Lordou Vironos Street, 6023 Larnaca, Cyprus
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">3. General Information and Mandatory Disclosures</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">Data Protection</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        The operators of these pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously.
        We treat your personal data confidentially and in accordance with statutory data protection
        regulations and this privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">Responsible Entity</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        The responsible entity for data processing on this website is:<br /><br />
        AVORIX GmbH<br />
        Managing Director: B&ouml;rge Penk<br />
        Email: info@avorix.de
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">4. Data Collection on This Website</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">Server Log Files</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        The website provider automatically collects and stores information in server log files
        that your browser automatically transmits. These are:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-2" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <li>Browser type and version</li>
        <li>Operating system used</li>
        <li>Referrer URL</li>
        <li>Host name of the accessing computer</li>
        <li>Time of the server request</li>
        <li>IP address</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        This data is not combined with other data sources. The basis for data processing
        is Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">Contact Form</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        If you send us inquiries via the contact form, your details from the inquiry form,
        including the contact data you provided, will be stored for the purpose of processing
        the inquiry and for follow-up questions. We will not share this data without your consent.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        If you have consented to the Marketing category and came to us via a Google ad, we additionally
        store the click identifier of this ad with your enquiry. Details can be found in the section
        "Google Ads Conversion Tracking".
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">Applications</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        If you apply to us, we process the data you provide: your contact details, your information on your professional experience and your preferred place of work, as well as any documents you send us voluntarily. We use this data exclusively to carry out the application process. The legal basis is Section 26(1) sentence 1 of the German Federal Data Protection Act (BDSG) in conjunction with Art. 88 GDPR: the processing is necessary for the decision on establishing an employment relationship. Where the data is also necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims, we base the processing on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest lies in particular in the legal review and defence of possible claims in connection with the application process.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        If you are not hired, we delete your application data no later than six months after the application process has been completed, unless longer storage is necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims. This period takes into account the deadlines for asserting possible claims under the German General Equal Treatment Act (AGG). As soon as the data is no longer required for these purposes, it is deleted. If you would like us to keep your documents for longer for future vacancies, we will ask you separately for your consent. You can withdraw this consent at any time with effect for the future. The lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal remains unaffected.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        If an employment relationship is established, we transfer the data to your personnel file.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        Applications sent via our website form are processed by our own form service on our own server; no external form provider is involved.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        If you have consented to the Marketing category and came to us via a Google ad, we additionally store the click identifier of this ad with your application. Details can be found in the section "Google Ads Conversion Tracking".
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 mb-4" style="color:var(--druck)">Contact via WhatsApp</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        On our job pages, we offer the option of writing to us via WhatsApp. WhatsApp is a service of WhatsApp Ireland Limited, Merrion Road, Dublin 4, D04 X2K5, Ireland. The link only opens WhatsApp once you tap it; no data is transmitted to WhatsApp before that. If you write to us, WhatsApp processes your phone number, your profile name, the message and technical data under its own responsibility in accordance with its own privacy policy; this may involve a transfer to the USA based on the adequacy decision of the European Commission (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework). We use your message solely to handle your application or enquiry. For applications, the legal basis and deletion periods in the section on applications apply. If you prefer not to use WhatsApp, you can reach us by phone, by email or via the form.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">5. Technically Necessary Local Storage</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        Your consent choice is stored as a technically necessary entry in your browser's local storage (<code>localStorage</code>) under the key <code>avorix_consent</code>. No data is transferred to third parties through this entry. The entry remains in your browser until you withdraw your consent, delete your browser data, or a technical renewal of the consent request occurs.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">6. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        This website does not set any analytics or marketing cookies by default. The optional categories are "Statistics" and "Marketing". Analytics services are only loaded if you consent to the Statistics category via our cookie banner, and the measurement of our ads only if you consent to the Marketing category. We do not use remarketing, i.e. addressing visitors again with advertising on other websites.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">7. Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics 4</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        When you consent to the Statistics category, we use Google Tag Manager and Google Analytics 4 provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Your consent under Art.&nbsp;6(1)(a) GDPR. Access to or storage of information on your device is based, where required, on your consent under Section&nbsp;25(1) TDDDG.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> Statistical reach and usage analysis. We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how our website is used and which content is helpful to visitors.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Data processed:</strong> Technical usage data, device information, event data and pseudonymous online identifiers may be processed.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>IP processing:</strong> According to Google, IP address data from users in the EU is used to derive approximate location information and is then deleted without being logged in Google Analytics.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Recipient:</strong> Google Ireland Limited. Processing outside the European Economic Area (EEA) may occur. The transfer to third countries is based on Standard Contractual Clauses adopted by the European Commission (Art.&nbsp;46(2)(c) GDPR) and additionally on the adequacy decision of the European Commission for the USA (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Storage duration:</strong> GA4 cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>) remain in the browser for up to 2 years under the currently used standard configuration. Event data is retained in the Avorix GA4 property for 14 months.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Google Consent Mode v2:</strong> We use Google Consent Mode v2 in Basic Mode. Without your consent, no cookies are set and no data is transferred to Google. The GTM script is only loaded once you have consented to at least one of the categories Statistics or Marketing. Google Analytics 4 is only triggered if you have consented to Statistics.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Withdrawal:</strong> You can withdraw your consent at any time via the "Cookie settings" link in the footer. The withdrawal applies for the future; data already transmitted is not retroactively deleted.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        We have concluded a data processing agreement with Google.
        Further information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="typo-link">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">8. Google Ads Conversion Tracking</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        When you consent to the Marketing category, we use Google Ads conversion tracking provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Legal basis:</strong> Your consent under Art.&nbsp;6(1)(a) GDPR. Access to or storage of information on your device is based on your consent under Section&nbsp;25(1) TDDDG.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> We run ads on Google. Conversion tracking shows us whether someone who came to our website via such an ad then sent an enquiry or application, downloaded a template or tapped our phone number. This tells us which ads work so we can allocate our advertising budget accordingly.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Data processed:</strong> the ad click identifier (GCLID), the time and type of the action, technical device and browser information and pseudonymous online identifiers. We do not transmit your name, your email address or the content of your enquiry to Google.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Click identifier, enquiry and application:</strong> If you came to us via a Google ad and consented to the Marketing category, we store the click identifier together with your enquiry or application. If the enquiry leads to an order or the application to a hiring, we may inform Google that an order or a hiring belongs to this click identifier. Only the click identifier and the time are transmitted, no contact details. The click identifier is deleted together with your enquiry or application.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Recipient:</strong> Google Ireland Limited. Google processes the data within Google Ads under its own responsibility. Processing outside the European Economic Area (EEA) may occur. The transfer to third countries is based on Standard Contractual Clauses adopted by the European Commission (Art.&nbsp;46(2)(c) GDPR) and additionally on the adequacy decision of the European Commission for the USA (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Storage duration:</strong> The cookies <code>_gcl_au</code> and <code>_gcl_aw</code> remain in your browser for up to 90&nbsp;days.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Google Consent Mode v2:</strong> We use Consent Mode in Basic Mode. Without your consent to the Marketing category, no Google Ads tags are triggered and no data is transferred to Google for advertising purposes.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        <strong>Withdrawal:</strong> You can withdraw your consent at any time via the "Cookie settings" link in the footer. The withdrawal applies for the future; data already transmitted is not retroactively deleted.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6" style="color:var(--grau)">
        Further information: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="typo-link">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 mb-6" style="color:var(--druck)">9. Your Rights</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--grau)">
        You have the right at any time to free information about your stored personal data,
        its origin and recipients, and the purpose of data processing, as well as a right to
        correction, blocking, or deletion of this data. You can contact us at any time regarding
        this and other questions about personal data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

